#: ../../../rest/db-need-get.rst:2
msgid "GET /rest/db/need"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../rest/db-need-get.rst:4
msgid ""
"Takes one mandatory parameter, ``folder``, and returns lists of files which "
"are needed by this device in order for it to become in sync."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../rest/db-need-get.rst:7
msgid ""
"The results can be paginated using the :ref:`common pagination parameters "
"<rest-pagination>`.  Pagination happens, across the union of all needed "
"files, that is - across all 3 sections of the response.  For example, given "
"the current need state is as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../rest/db-need-get.rst:12
msgid "``progress`` has 15 items"
msgstr "``progress`` 有 15 個項目"

#: ../../../rest/db-need-get.rst:13
msgid "``queued`` has 3 items"
msgstr "``queued`` 有 3 個項目"

#: ../../../rest/db-need-get.rst:14
msgid "``rest`` has 12 items"
msgstr "``rest`` 有 12 個項目"

#: ../../../rest/db-need-get.rst:16
msgid ""
"If you issue a query with ``page=1`` and ``perpage=10``, only the "
"``progress`` section in the response will have 10 items. If you issue a "
"request query with ``page=2`` and ``perpage=10``, ``progress`` section will "
"have the last 5 items, ``queued`` section will have all 3 items, and "
"``rest`` section will have first 2 items. If you issue a query for "
"``page=3`` and ``perpage=10``, you will only have the last 10 items of the "
"``rest`` section."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../rest/db-need-get.rst:23
msgid ""
"Return format changed in version 0.14.43, removing the ``total`` count "
"attribute."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../rest/db-need-get.rst:26
msgid ""
"{\n"
"  # Files currently being downloaded\n"
"  \"progress\": [\n"
"    {\n"
"      \"flags\": \"0755\",\n"
"      \"sequence\": 6,\n"
"      \"modified\": \"2015-04-20T23:06:12+09:00\",\n"
"      \"name\": \"ls\",\n"
"      \"size\": 34640,\n"
"      \"version\": [\n"
"        \"5157751870738175669:1\"\n"
"      ]\n"
"    }\n"
"  ],\n"
"  # Files queued to be downloaded next (as per array order)\n"
"  \"queued\": [\n"
"      ...\n"
"  ],\n"
"  # Files to be downloaded after all queued files will be downloaded.\n"
"  # This happens when we start downloading files, and new files get added "
"while we are downloading.\n"
"  \"rest\": [\n"
"      ...\n"
"  ],\n"
"  \"page\": 1,\n"
"  \"perpage\": 100\n"
"}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../rest/db-need-get.rst:55
msgid ""
"This is an expensive call, increasing CPU and RAM usage on the device. Use "
"sparingly."
msgstr ""
